{
  "version": 4,
  "about": "Test vectors of the nslookup install agent protocol (/agent/v1). Every key and join code in this file is a fixed test value used nowhere else. Both the engine and the agent test against this file; it changes only with the protocol, and every change raises version (2: answers name the agent and the request line, and a join proves its code without sending the secret; 3: the join proof and the join MAC are labelled NSA1-JOIN-REQ / NSA1-JOIN-ANS; 4: a removed agent gets a signed 403 {\"code\":\"agent_removed\"}, every answer names the key that signed it (signedBy), and heartbeat answers list serverSignPublicKeys for a server key rollover).",
  "format": {
    "encoding": "Raw keys, seeds, signatures, nonces, salts, shared secrets, bundle keys and sealed parts are base64url without padding; sha256 values are lowercase hex.",
    "text": "body, requestBody, responseBody, plaintext, canonical and aad are UTF-8 text: hash, sign, MAC and encrypt their UTF-8 bytes. *Hex fields are the exact bytes, hex-encoded.",
    "ed25519": "seed = the 32-byte RFC 8032 private key (Go: ed25519.NewKeyFromSeed); publicKey = the raw 32 bytes; signatures are 64 bytes.",
    "x25519": "privateKey = the raw 32-byte scalar (Go: ecdh.X25519().NewPrivateKey); publicKey = the raw 32 bytes.",
    "requests": "canonical = \"NSA1\\n<method>\\n<pathWithQuery>\\n<timestamp>\\n<nonce>\\n<agentId>\\n<bodySha256>\"; signature = Ed25519(keys.agentSign, canonical).",
    "answers": "canonical = \"NSA1-RESP\\n<status>\\n<agentId>\\n<method>\\n<pathWithQuery>\\n<requestNonce>\\n<bodySha256>\"; signature = Ed25519(keys[signedBy], canonical). agentId, method, pathWithQuery and requestNonce are those of the request answered, exactly as it was signed. Signed answers are the 2xx ones and the 403 whose body is exactly {\"code\":\"agent_removed\"} (the agent idles only on that body with a signature that verifies; any other 403, or one unsigned or badly signed, is a transient error).",
    "joinCodes": "A join code is \"nsj_\" + 12 base62 + \"_\" + 36 base62 (base62 = 0-9A-Za-z, nothing else, no surrounding whitespace). joinCodeId = the part before the last \"_\" (sent in the JoinRequest); secret = the last 36 characters (never sent). valid: each joinCode splits into joinCodeId and secret; invalid: none of these strings is a join code.",
    "joins": "requestBody = the JoinRequest exactly as sent; proofMessage = the ASCII bytes of \"NSA1-JOIN-REQ\\n\" followed by the UTF-8 bytes of requestBody (proofMessageHex); proof (header x-nsa-join-proof) = hex HMAC-SHA256(key = UTF-8 bytes of secret, message = proofMessage). responseBody = the 201 JoinResponse exactly as sent; macMessage = the ASCII bytes of \"NSA1-JOIN-ANS\\n\" followed by the UTF-8 bytes of responseBody (macMessageHex); mac (header x-nsa-join-mac) = hex HMAC-SHA256(key = UTF-8 bytes of secret, message = macMessage). The two labels keep a request and its proof from ever verifying as an answer, and the other way round.",
    "seals": "epk = X25519 public of ephemeralPrivateKey; sharedSecret = X25519(ephemeralPrivateKey, keys.agentSeal.publicKey) = X25519(keys.agentSeal.privateKey, epk); salt = epk raw || keys.agentSeal.publicKey raw; bundleKey = HKDF-SHA256(ikm = sharedSecret, salt, info = \"nslookup-agent bundle key v1\", 32 bytes); aad = \"<assignmentId>|<sha256>\"; ciphertext = AES-256-GCM(bundleKey, nonce, plaintext, aad) followed by the 16-byte tag (Go: cipher.AEAD Seal output). ephemeralPrivateKey and nonce are fixed here only so the output is reproducible; real seals use fresh random ones.",
    "serverSignPublicKeys": "A heartbeat answer lists serverSignPublicKeys: 1 or 2 raw 32-byte Ed25519 public keys, base64url; [0] signs current answers, [1] (during a rotation) is the next key. An agent accepts an answer signed by any key it trusts (first the join's serverSignPublicKey); after a heartbeat answer verifies, it replaces its trusted set with the list when the list is valid: 1-2 entries, each well formed and not of small order, including the key that verified the answer. keys.serverSignNext is the next key of these vectors."
  },
